And when we got to Frankfurt, we had to change trains, because we were on our way to Italy, to Genoa, where we were going to take the American ship that brought us to the United States. And when we got off the train from Idstein in Frankfurt that night, they have these-- these-- these newspaper stands from various surrounding cities.

Wiesbaden was about maybe 20, 30 kilometers from us, Frankfurt a little further. So right up there was the Idstein[NON-ENGLISH], which was the newspaper from Idstein. And in huge headline, it said, 'Idstein Judenfrei,' which translates into no more Jews in Idstein. OK. So that was my last memory of Idstein as I left. [PAUSES FOR 5 SECONDS]

I do remember prior to that, I mean, I-- if-- if I-- something's coming to mind. If I can just cut here and go back, if you don't mind.

